.TH CVECTOR_APPEND_CVECTOR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_append_cvector \- append a vector to a vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

bool cvector_append_cvector(cvec v_to, cvec v_from);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function appends all the elements of one vector to another vector.
Both vectors must have the same element size.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v_to    Destination vector
v_from  Source vector
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Gives true on success
Gives false when the combined element count overflows or is more than
ccol_max_elem_count
Gives false when the memory allocation fails
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The two element sizes must be the same. The function asserts when they
are different.
The function appends all the elements or none of them.
The function reserves more capacity automatically when this is
necessary.
The function asserts when v_to or v_from is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_append_cvec (3),
.BR cvector_append_array (3)
